<attribute name="refinedDescription" nodeId="94c8a6e5">&lt;p&gt;
    Decide what to monitor and how often. Make sure project team has the required skills to address issues. Supplement the
    RAID log with a process for dealing with issue control.&amp;nbsp; This process helps the project team understand what to do
    with issues once they have been identified.&amp;nbsp; The control issue framework should answer questions such as:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        How will responsibility be assigned&amp;nbsp;for resolving the issue? For example, is there one person who handles all
        technical issues? Who would handle a vendor issue?
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        How will&amp;nbsp;the team&amp;nbsp;know when to escalate an issue to management or the steering committee? Consider
        creating a matrix of potential business impact versus issue complexity to help decide which issues should be taken
        to higher levels of management.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Which criteria will determine an issue&apos;s priority status?
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Who will set the target resolution date?
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        How will issues be communicated within the team? Will&amp;nbsp;the team&amp;nbsp;use regular meetings, log checks, status
        update emails, and so on?
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        How different issues be segregated&amp;nbsp;if several occur during one project? It is helpful to number them so that
        you can identify issues easily when discussing them in progress meetings.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        If change orders are needed, how will those be handled?
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        When the resolution affects the budget or schedule, what will the update process be, and who will be responsible?
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Perform variance analysis, comparing plan against actual project values, that may reveal problems that require
    intervention. Evaluate action plan progress against issue resolution goals&amp;nbsp;and adjust to resolve.&amp;nbsp;
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
</Element>
